Dr. Khalifa: He established Bahaism. Yeah. Ismail Barakat: Ah, yeah, yeah.

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:35.000
He, he... I mean, it's easy for him to know that. It's very easy for him to know that.

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:43.000
Satan probably knew... In that other dimension, Satan probably knows that all God's creation has the 19 on it.

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:47.000
And then, he reads in the Quran, [74:30] On it are nineteen.

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:51.000
So, I mean, he's not stupid, by no means.

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:55.000
Dr. Khalifa: He's very stupid, I'm sorry, but I mean, the relative.

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:57.000
A man: He's sly. He's sly.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:17:02.000
Dr. Khalifa: He's very stupid for thinking that he can be a god. A man: He's sly on (unintelligible) A woman: He's not intelligent but he has a lot of knowledge.

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:04.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes. A woman: His knowledge (unintelligible).

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:10.000
Dr. Khalifa: Of course, of course. I mean, he's just overestimating his powers. And...

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:19.000
God did not give him... Actually, God is giving him another chance to prove that.

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:23.000
Dr. Khalifa: But he knows better than making such a claim.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:24.000
A man: So, the fact that, for...

00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:31.000
Dr. Khalifa: There are many, many, many millions of creatures like Satan in God's kingdom. But he's the only one who went off.

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:38.000
A man: The fact that 20,000 children are dying every day in the world of starvation, actually makes Satan really annoyed.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:40.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:42.000
A man: Because it proves every day that he's really incompetent. Dr. Khalifa: Because he's incompetent.

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:56.000
Dr. Khalifa: Exactly, exactly. But again, back to God's Mercy, to give us 40 years, is really giving us the flimsiest excuses to save us, redeem us, take us to Heaven.

00:17:58.000 --> 00:18:06.000
The people who live beyond 40 and then fight God had to be very bad as far as that blasphemy was concerned.

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:16.000
So, if any of us had an atom of leaning towards God during that big feud, God apparently is saving all those people.

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:20.000
Dr. Khalifa: And there are millions, and we'll be so thankful in the Hereafter.

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:26.000
A woman: Mã Shã Allãh. Excuse me, what would be Sheytan's punishment?

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:29.000
Dr. Khalifa: Exile from God's kingdom.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.000
Dr. Khalifa: Hell.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:36.000
A woman: I mean, but he's made of fire himself. So, I mean, Hell wouldn't hurt him.

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:37.000
Dr. Khalifa: Hell is not fire.

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:39.000
A woman: Not fire.

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:43.000
Dr. Khalifa: See, remember Hell and Heaven are allegories.

00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:45.000
Ismail Barakat: Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala...

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:47.000
Dr. Khalifa: Who?

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:49.000
A man: (unintelligible)

00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:51.000
Dr. Khalifa: It's 1:30. The plane leaves at what time?

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:53.000
A man: 2:30. Yes.

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:54.000
Dr. Khalifa: You have one hour.

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:57.000
Dr. Khalifa: See, another good surprise. Where's Parivash?

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:05.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:10.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:14.000
Dr. Khalifa: Let's listen to Feroz's question.

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:16.000
Dr. Khalifa: What did you say?

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:19.000
Feroz: Isn't there a verse in the Quran that says that the devils are forbidden from understanding Quran?

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:23.000
Dr. Khalifa: On this dimension. In this dimension.

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:28.000
Feroz: What about the jinns? They don't know. Because they heard Moses... Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:31.000
Ismail Barakat: (72:1) سَمِعْنَا قُرْءَانًا عَجَبًۭا Feroz: They don't know the Quran, right? Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:32.000
Ismail Barakat: (72:2) يَهْدِىٓ إِلَى ٱلرُّشْدِ Dr. Khalifa: Right.

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:33.000
Feroz: But Satan does?

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.000
Dr. Khalifa: Oh, Oh, this is exactly the example I was looking for.

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:43.000
Dr. Khalifa: We were talking this morning, is it the same people, we were talking about how, when the prophet Muhammad said

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:48.000
"Say, I'm afraid if I disobey my Lord, I'm afraid of a terrible retribution."

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:50.000
Ismail Barakat: "The retribution on a terrible day." Dr. Khalifa: How many people did we discuss this with?

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:54.000
Dr. Khalifa: And I was looking for an example where Qul (قل) "say" means it is done.

00:19:55.000 --> 00:20:01.000
So, the verse is saying [72:1] Say, "I was inspired that a number of jinns listened to ... the Quran.

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:04.000
And they went to their people.

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:08.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, this is something I was involved in. Ismail Barakat: (72:1) قُلْ أُوحِىَ إِلَىَّ أَنَّهُ

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:10.000
Dr. Khalifa: This is a good example. It was already done. I didn't need... It says,

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:11.000
قُلْ أُوحِىَ إِلَىَّ

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:16.000
"Say, I was inspired to say that a number of jinns listened to the Quran, and this was already happened, done.

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:26.000
So, I was saying that when the prophet Muhammad was ordered to say "I'm afraid if I disobey my Lord"

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:30.000
Oh, Muhammad, it was you.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:36.000
Remember you asked the question if Muhammad's property belonged to the state or to his children, and there was fight,

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:41.000
and I told you, you will not find anything that Muhammad took for himself.

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:46.000
And I was positive about that because of that verse.

00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:53.000
Dr. Khalifa: He will see to it that nothing entered his pocket that was not belonging to him, that belonged to the state or...

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:54.000
Ismail Barakat: That he was not entitled to.

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:56.000
Dr. Khalifa: Right, exactly.

00:20:56.000 --> 00:21:05.000
Because Muhammad was telling me a Hadith and Sunnah story that after the prophet died, they were fighting over who inherits his property. Is it the state or his children?

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:08.000
Ismail Barakat: Not all of his property, Rashad. It was only certain property.

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:12.000
Dr. Khalifa: No, none of it. None of it. He did not have any property that was not his.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:16.000
Ismail Barakat: But the fight was specifically over that... Dr. Khalifa: There was no fight.

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:21.000
Dr. Khalifa: See, we have, we must learn not to take off on a Hadith story or something.

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:26.000
You cannot make an assumption. Somebody says this is red.

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:30.000
And then, you go on discussing why it is red because the assumption itself is wrong.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:31.000
Dr. Khalifa: Muhammad.

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:36.000
Muhammad: Yeah. You said "Hell is not fire." What is Hell?

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:41.000
Dr. Khalifa: Hell is exile from God and not having...

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:46.000
Dr. Khalifa: First of all, we have no way of comprehending how, what Heaven is and what Hell is.

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:50.000
A man: Hell is hate and Heaven is love.

00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:55.000
Dr. Khalifa: Hell is exile from God. It's exile that is farther from this earth.

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:58.000
Dr. Khalifa: Wake up. You mustn't sleep.

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:04.000
Ismail Barakat: No, I'm listening to what you're saying. You're saying that Hell is exile from God. Dr. Khalifa: I want you to understand...

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:06.000
Dr. Khalifa: I want you to understand this very... Look. Listen to this carefully.

00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:11.000
Dr. Khalifa: We are here in the seventh universe, in the heart of the seventh universe.

00:22:11.000 --> 00:22:16.000
And you can see how many problems the people have. Alcoholism, accidents, divorce, miseries.

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:23.000
There will be an eighth universe on the Day of Judgment. The eighth universe will be Hell.

00:22:24.000 --> 00:22:26.000
Can you imagine how far it will be?

00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:31.000
This is why God says "we're gonna fold the heavens and the earth like the folding of a book."

00:22:32.000 --> 00:22:35.000
And then in Sura 14, God says "I will create new heavens and new earth."

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:38.000
And this time there will be eight of them, not seven.

00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:41.000
They'll probably be much bigger.

00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:45.000
And the eighth universe will be much farther from God. So that's Hell.

00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:48.000
It will be much worse.

00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:52.000
We have no way of comprehending how bad it is.

00:22:52.000 --> 00:23:02.000
See, even, now in this seventh universe, God is taking care of all the provisions, providing for all the ants and the horses and the people.

00:23:02.000 --> 00:23:04.000
But in the eighth universe there is no such thing.

00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:12.000
The people will be in the new form of butterflies instead of caterpillars.

00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:15.000
There'll be different kinds of...

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:18.000
Dr. Khalifa: And they will try to come to the seventh universe.

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:26.000
Parivash: That means that the people who are going to Hell, instead of going up, they're falling down.

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:31.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes, yes, farther, yes. Yes, exactly, exactly.

00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:33.000
Dr. Khalifa: Exactly.

00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:39.000
A woman: So, Rashad, what's the meaning when in the Quran says that you will be the ones who are

00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:43.000
in Hell, you will be burned and then re-burn again and then re-burn again?

00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:43.000
Ismail Barakat: There is no death.

00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:45.000
A woman: What does that mean?

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:46.000
Dr. Khalifa: It's all allegorical.

00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:50.000
All the descriptions of Hell and Heaven in the Quran are allegorical, all of them.

00:23:50.000 --> 00:23:57.000
But you get glimpses of what it is like, like in Sura 57, when the hypocrites come and try to beg for light.

00:23:58.000 --> 00:23:59.000
This means energy.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:03.000
Dr. Khalifa: Go take a nap. Come on, go.

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:15.000
Feroz: It should be more like, It will be more like in a sense, like angels that travel from the high universes that travel all the way down here.

00:24:15.000 --> 00:24:19.000
Feroz: And the Quran says that the believers will go down and meet people. Dr. Khalifa: We'll go visit

00:24:19.000 --> 00:24:21.000
Dr. Khalifa: our friends and relatives in Hell.

00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:23.000
Ismail Barakat: That is most people you know.

00:24:24.000 --> 00:24:25.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:24:26.000 --> 00:24:28.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes. It's gonna be fantastic.

00:24:28.000 --> 00:24:35.000
That, that day of, this Eternal Day of the real life is going to be fantastic. Because it's everything...

00:24:35.000 --> 00:24:40.000
You're walking around now as a king or queen on earth, but nobody knows you,

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:42.000
which is wonderful, because you don't need secret service guards.

00:24:46.000 --> 00:24:49.000
Dr. Khalifa: We go to the subway in Washington, D.C., walking among the people.

00:24:50.000 --> 00:24:52.000
There are actually guards around you.

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:55.000
Sometimes it happens literally, like with Ihsan.

00:24:55.000 --> 00:24:58.000
She was going to Africa, Sierra Leone.

00:24:58.000 --> 00:25:06.000
I told her they will, so that you're (اميرة الامراء), you know, a servant of God and a princess, and they will meet you

00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:12.000
with red carpets and 21-gun salute and the lines of soldiers and so on.

00:25:12.000 --> 00:25:19.000
And soon enough she went to Africa and landed, and there's the red carpet and 21-gun salute and the soldiers and lines.

00:25:20.000 --> 00:25:23.000
And they thought they were meeting the president of Gambia, you know, who was on the same plane with her.

00:25:26.000 --> 00:25:28.000
Ihsan: (Unintelligible) They were traveling with me.

00:25:32.000 --> 00:25:34.000
Ihsan: (Unintelligible) traveling with us.

00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:43.000
(unintelligible) another day.

00:25:43.000 --> 00:25:49.000
So, he said (unintelligible)

00:25:49.000 --> 00:25:51.000
There is a private secret service.

00:25:51.000 --> 00:25:58.000
Ihsan: (unintelligible) and the 21-gun salutes will do it. (unintelligible)

00:25:58.000 --> 00:26:01.000
Dr. Khalifa: She told... Oh, you told her your granddaughter is a college student?

00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:02.000
Ihsan: Yes.

00:26:02.000 --> 00:26:03.000
Dr. Khalifa: She's a college student.

00:26:07.000 --> 00:26:10.000
Dr. Khalifa: And she probably thought that, I'm just thinking highly of you.

00:26:10.000 --> 00:26:16.000
Ihsan: Yes, and I tell her how nice you are, how high you think of me, how you describe this.

00:26:16.000 --> 00:26:24.000
Ihsan: And after a while, from London, here comes a lot of people, promotions, (unintelligible) checking everybody sitting behind a chair and said,

00:26:24.000 --> 00:26:27.000
Ihsan: and then said "what's happening?" I said "The VIP and the..."

00:26:28.000 --> 00:26:29.000
Dr. Khalifa: That's right.

00:26:31.000 --> 00:26:34.000
Ihsan: "VIP", just like this. She said "VIP." They will not say who or...

00:26:36.000 --> 00:26:37.000
Dr. Khalifa: We know. Ihsan: We know.

00:26:38.000 --> 00:26:47.000
Ihsan: But then, they have a carpet. The red carpet was there, and the music, and the 21-gun salute, and the leader of Gambia was traveling with us.

00:26:47.000 --> 00:26:49.000
Dr. Khalifa: But she didn't say what Sunayta said.

00:26:49.000 --> 00:26:52.000
So, they are landing, imagine her granddaughter, they're landing, and there's the red carpet,

00:26:52.000 --> 00:26:54.000
and the 21-gun salute, and things that we said.

00:26:54.000 --> 00:26:57.000
She said "Grandma, Grandma, they are doing it."

00:26:58.000 --> 00:27:01.000
Isamil Barakat: (unintelligible) Dr. Khalifa: Rashad was right.

00:27:08.000 --> 00:27:09.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yeah.

00:27:10.000 --> 00:27:11.000
Dr. Khalifa: This is what you said?

00:27:12.000 --> 00:27:13.000
Dr. Khalifa: Oh, yeah.

00:27:15.000 --> 00:27:16.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes, Muhammad.

00:27:16.000 --> 00:27:24.000
Muhammad: Yes. Rashad, Sura 101, it says here in Arabic,

00:27:25.000 --> 00:27:31.000
(101:8) وَأَمَّا مَنْ خَفَّتْ مَوَٰزِينُهُۥ (101:9) فَأُمُّهُۥ هَاوِيَةٌۭ (101:10) وَمَآ أَدْرَىٰكَ مَا هِيَهْ

00:27:31.000 --> 00:27:33.000
Dr. Khalifa: Muhammad: (101:11) نَارٌ حَامِيَةٌۢ

00:27:33.000 --> 00:27:33.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:27:33.000 --> 00:27:36.000
Muhammad: That Narun (نَارٌ) and Jahim (جَحِيمَ) Dr. Khalifa: Yes, yes.

00:27:36.000 --> 00:27:40.000
Muhammad: And in Sura 102 (102:6) لَتَرَوُنَّ ٱلْجَحِيمَ

00:27:40.000 --> 00:27:41.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:27:41.000 --> 00:27:44.000
Muhammad: which is translated here to [102:6] You would envision Hell.

00:27:44.000 --> 00:27:45.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:27:45.000 --> 00:27:47.000
Muhammad: And this [101:11] The blazing Hellfire.

00:27:47.000 --> 00:27:48.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:27:48.000 --> 00:27:50.000
Dr. Khalifa: It's all allegorical, all of it.

00:27:51.000 --> 00:27:58.000
You see, the first, yeah, the first... At the very beginning of the Quran, when God talked about Heaven and Hell, He told us this is allegorical.

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:05.000
Yes, they're all allegorical. There's no, it's not fire. It's mostly darkness, actually.

00:28:07.000 --> 00:28:10.000
Dr. Khalifa: Mostly darkness. Remember, "we need some of your light."

00:28:11.000 --> 00:28:13.000
Feroz: Spiritual darkness or actual physical darkness?

00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:14.000
Dr. Khalifa: Both.

00:28:14.000 --> 00:28:16.000
A man: Both (unintelligible) Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:28:17.000 --> 00:28:22.000
Dr. Khalifa: Because the eighth universe, God will not give them stars or anything.

00:28:23.000 --> 00:28:29.000
Parivash: Yes, and it's just a proof that if Sheytan is from fire, and Hell is fire, it doesn't hurt him. Dr. Khalifa: Yeah,

00:28:29.000 --> 00:28:31.000
Dr. Khalifa: he'd enjoy it. No, it'd be a little provision.

00:28:32.000 --> 00:28:38.000
No, it's not fire at all, and Heaven is not trees and spouses and food, fruit.

00:28:38.000 --> 00:28:40.000
Dr. Khalifa: It's indescribably fantastic.

00:28:41.000 --> 00:28:46.000
Feroz: Maybe, Hell will be very cold because so far, no stars, and Sheytan, you know, Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:28:46.000 --> 00:28:48.000
Feroz: made of fire in the cold where is...

00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:49.000
Dr. Khalifa: Exactly. Here we go.

00:28:53.000 --> 00:29:01.000
Dr. Khalifa: You see, we understand a lot from, from the, understand, we have quite a bit of information, you know, in the Quran.

00:29:01.000 --> 00:29:09.000
When we learn that we can go and visit our relatives and friends, and they will be coming around us like butterflies go around the light.

00:29:09.000 --> 00:29:20.000
Imagine a thousand acres of Alfalfa, what is that? Clover? I was gonna say clover.

00:29:20.000 --> 00:29:21.000
Alfalfa, for example.

00:29:21.000 --> 00:29:29.000
There's millions of butterflies, and it's pitch dark in that one thousand acres, and then you send the light.

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:31.000
Huh?

00:29:33.000 --> 00:29:34.000
Right.

00:29:34.000 --> 00:29:39.000
So, we will go there, and we're gonna visit, and they will come and they will beg for light.

00:29:40.000 --> 00:29:46.000
Dr. Khalifa: And we'll go and meet them, and we will talk to them, and we'll say "thank God that I didn't listen to you."

00:29:47.000 --> 00:29:50.000
Feroz: Will we have any remorse? Dr. Khalifa: It's Sura 37. Never. No.

00:29:51.000 --> 00:29:54.000
Dr. Khalifa: Ok. This is another point. "Will we have any remorse? Will you feel sorry for them?"

00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:57.000
A woman: What is "remorse"? A woman: Sadness. Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:29:57.000 --> 00:29:59.000
A woman: Sadness. Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:02.000
Dr. Khalifa: We will not feel sorry for them. There'll be no sorrow at all.

00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:05.000
Feroz: Even if they're good friends or relatives or whatever?

00:30:05.000 --> 00:30:13.000
Dr. Khalifa: Even if they are the best of friends, because you realize they well deserved what they wanted, and that they insisted on going there.

00:30:15.000 --> 00:30:19.000
I loved my father very much. He loved me very much all our lives.

00:30:19.000 --> 00:30:28.000
Dr. Khalifa: But I don't feel sorry for him, because he was fighting God actively, and he insisted on going to Hell.

00:30:29.000 --> 00:30:30.000
A man: He wanted it.

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:33.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yeah, he wanted it bad. I mean,

00:30:33.000 --> 00:30:37.000
Because I talked to him here for four months in this masjid.

00:30:38.000 --> 00:30:43.000
And the last, one of the times, he stood out here, outside the mosque.

00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:48.000
"I'm not going in this masjid unless you add Muhammad to the Azan (Call to Prayer).

00:30:49.000 --> 00:30:50.000
Yes.

00:30:50.000 --> 00:30:54.000
I said "then, you cannot come in here because the idol worshippers are filth."

00:30:55.000 --> 00:31:00.000
Dr. Khalifa: I had to use that expression from the Quran. Ismail Barakat: Subhan Allah.

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:03.000
Dr. Khalifa: I said "this is idol worship. You're not satisfied with God alone. So..."

00:31:03.000 --> 00:31:07.000
I'm giving you an example of my own father, because I really loved him immensely.

00:31:08.000 --> 00:31:13.000
And I was his favorite for a long time until I said "God alone."

00:31:13.000 --> 00:31:15.000
Ismail Barakat: (9:28) إِنَّمَا ٱلْمُشْرِكُونَ نَجَسٌۭ

00:31:15.000 --> 00:31:18.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes, I mean, he went to extremes.

00:31:18.000 --> 00:31:24.000
He went from loving me excessively to calling someone to have me put away, prisoned or killed.

00:31:24.000 --> 00:31:27.000
Then, he died 19 days later.

00:31:29.000 --> 00:31:33.000
So, we will not feel sorry for them because they insisted on it. This is what they wanted.

